  "reason": "The current best is config_039 (0.7250) with scvi_n200 + imagenet_vit_l + multiprofile + transformer + weighted. All four aggregation×fusion combinations for this exact model setting are now tested, confirming transformer+weighted is optimal. The key remaining uncertainty is how much the image encoder quality contributes in the multimodal setting: resnet50 alone scored only 0.208, yet imagenet_vit_l in multimodal adds ~7% over RNA-only. Config_033 (scvi_n200 + resnet50 + multiprofile + transformer + weighted) isolates the image-encoder effect while holding all other parameters at their best-known values, making it the cleanest single-variable comparison to config_039. It is the highest-expected-performance untested configuration given that scvi_n200, multiprofile, transformer, and weighted are all confirmed as the best settings for their respective axes. As the final experiment, it either confirms imagenet_vit_l is essential to the 0.7250 result or reveals that the RNA encoder dominates, either way maximizing our understanding of the best achievable accuracy within budget."
}

